  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=213 head=ebba143d7d4cfa2eed49a34a0dc15ebf6535bf1b -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 213 @ ebba143d7d4c\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-09T04:37:31Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-116-expanded-line-measurements` onto `main`; merge base `a111c34ab3ca8b0db115b73156ddcd5bf886e9f8`; head `ebba143d7d4cfa2eed49a34a0dc15ebf6535bf1b`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Observables/LineMeasurement/Expanded.lean:40` \u2014 Reuse the imported tensor-sum lemmas instead of reproving their content entrywise.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:1645` \u2014 The new `lineTauMeas` link has no matching definition of its two-outcome product measurement.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Observables/LineMeasurement/SquareRootError.lean:57` \u2014 \u201cSquare-summable\u201d omits the normalization assumptions needed for the stated bound.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Observables/LineMeasurement/Expanded.lean:34` \u2014 Remove implementation-visibility and relocation history from the mathematical docstring.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Observables/LineMeasurement/LinePointOverlap.lean:117` \u2014 Replace \u201coption-valued families\u201d with mathematical terminology for completed measurements.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\n**F1:** `heteroKron_sum_sum` unfolds `Matrix.kroneckerMap` to rederive distributivity already provided by `DistanceCalculus.heteroKron_finset_sum_left` and `heteroKron_finset_sum_right` in `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistanceTheorems/Support.lean:253` and `:263`. These declarations are available through the existing import. I verified that composing them proves this exact statement. Replace the entrywise proof with those public lemmas; the broader consolidation tracked by #204 is unnecessary for this repair. This requires changes under the requested API-reuse and duplication rules.\n\n**Statement Integrity:** No mathematical or source-statement blocker found. `lem:qld-comm-line-cons` in `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:523` requires projective expanded measurements and three polynomial-error consistency conclusions, including symmetric equivalents. The Lean declarations retain the projective winning-strategy assumptions, universal constants preceding parameter quantifiers, all four directed placements, and the final `\u221a\u03b5` error. No proof-obligation assumptions were added. The completed evaluation classes follow blueprint `def:ideg-deg-polynomials`; the stronger intermediate linear estimates are justified by the summed overlap identity and projective refinement.\n\n**Verification:** Direct checks passed for `LineMeasurement.lean`, `LinePointOverlap.lean`, and `EvalClassConsistency.lean`. No proof holes or prohibited bypasses were found in the expanded-line modules. Axiom checks for `exists_deltaLine`, projectivity, and axis-degree vanishing returned only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. `git diff --check` passed; the checkout remains unchanged.\n\nFull-project and blueprint builds were not rerun. The external `lean-conventions` reference was unavailable locally; repository conventions were inspected.\n\n## Prose review\n\n**F1: Blueprint correspondence.** The definition at blueprint line 1655 describes the convolution measurement indexed by a single polynomial \\(f\\). However, [Expanded.lean:180](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-116-expanded-line-current/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Observables/LineMeasurement/Expanded.lean:180) defines `lineTauMeas` with separate outcomes \\((f',f'')\\) and effects \\(M_{f'}\\otimes\\tau_{f''}\\). The newly linked object is neither the convolution nor the ancillary measurement already described. Introduce this product measurement explicitly, preferably in a subordinate definition analogous to `def:point-tau-measurement`, and connect it through the appropriate `\\uses` links.\n\n**F2: Mathematical terminology.** \u201cThe squared distance between two square-summable operator families is at most four\u201d is false without normalization: singleton families \\(A=3I\\), \\(B=0\\) give squared distance \\(9\\) on a unit vector. The signature correctly assumes \\(\\sum_a A_a^\\dagger A_a\\leq I\\) and \\(\\sum_a B_a^\\dagger B_a\\leq I\\). Replace \u201csquare-summable\u201d with those explicit conditions.\n\n**F3: Implementation prose.** The phrase \u201cit is `private` and therefore invisible from this file; consolidating the two copies\u2026\u201d describes implementation organization, not mathematics. Retain the tensor-product identity and source citation; move the visibility and relocation discussion to the audit note. Apply the same treatment to the relocation narrative at lines 50\u201353.\n\n**F4: Lean terminology.** Replace \u201cEffects of the option-valued families\u201d with \u201cEffects of the completed measurement families.\u201d The operators are not option-valued; their outcome sets have an additional non-evaluation outcome.\n\nSummary: **1 blueprint correspondence mismatch and 3 prose issues.** The main consistency statements match the corrected blueprint, without additional proof-obligation hypotheses. Read-only axiom checks support the new proof-level `\\leanok`; the general symmetry-transfer `\\notready` remains appropriate.\n\nValidation used the checkout at the specified head, source comparison, label resolution, and targeted axiom reports. No files changed; full compilation and blueprint rendering were not rerun.\n",
